WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.901
Levels three to five spent their time estimating a spread, because for

2
00:00:05.001 --> 00:00:09.332
a measurement the spread is a separate fact about the process.

3
00:00:09.416 --> 00:00:14.844
Count defective items instead, and that stops being true. Out of n

4
00:00:14.944 --> 00:00:20.957
items the number defective is binomial, and its standard deviation is the

5
00:00:21.057 --> 00:00:25.396
square root of n, times p bar, times one minus p bar.

6
00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:28.334
Divide by n to turn the count into a

7
00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:31.695
fraction, and the n moves under the root.

8
00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:35.655
Nothing on the right is a separate spread. The rate and

9
00:00:35.755 --> 00:00:39.627
the subgroup size fix it, and nobody gets to choose it.

10
00:00:39.716 --> 00:00:43.282
Here is a subgroup of two hundred items at four

11
00:00:43.382 --> 00:00:47.416
per cent defective: how often each fraction turns up.

12
00:00:47.516 --> 00:00:51.040
Three sigma either side gives the limits.

13
00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:54.061
Now move the rate, and only the rate. The

14
00:00:54.161 --> 00:00:57.753
spread follows it, because the rate is the spread.

15
00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:02.886
At fifty per cent the scatter is as wide as it can ever get.

16
00:01:02.983 --> 00:01:06.643
Bring the rate down to two per cent and the band

17
00:01:06.743 --> 00:01:11.187
closes up. The lower limit runs into zero and stops there.

18
00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:15.848
The arithmetic puts it below zero, at minus one per cent.

19
00:01:15.948 --> 00:01:20.595
A chart cannot draw a negative fraction, so it draws zero,

20
00:01:20.695 --> 00:01:23.951
and a limit at zero can never be crossed.

21
00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:27.109
That is why a chart for counts has no range

22
00:01:27.209 --> 00:01:31.078
chart beside it. There is no separate spread to chart.

23
00:01:31.166 --> 00:01:33.746
Now hold the rate at four per cent,

24
00:01:33.846 --> 00:01:37.114
and change the size of the subgroup instead.

25
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.828
Fifty items per subgroup, and the band opens wide.

26
00:01:41.916 --> 00:01:45.640
Two hundred, and it closes. A bigger subgroup gives a

27
00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:50.041
steadier fraction, so when the size changes from one subgroup

28
00:01:50.141 --> 00:01:53.504
to the next, the limits have to breathe with it.

29
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.685
Even at two hundred the lower limit is stuck at zero.

30
00:01:57.785 --> 00:02:00.923
The rule of thumb says n p bar of five is

31
00:02:01.023 --> 00:02:05.188
enough, which here is a hundred and twenty five items.

32
00:02:05.283 --> 00:02:12.143
The arithmetic says otherwise. The limit clears zero only from 217.

33
00:02:12.233 --> 00:02:17.564
Look closely at the floor. Above that size, every item you add buys a

34
00:02:17.664 --> 00:02:22.837
real lower limit: a chart that can tell you the process got better.

35
00:02:22.933 --> 00:02:25.893
A limit at zero is not a limit. Size

36
00:02:25.993 --> 00:02:29.889
the subgroup so the chart can signal both ways.

